# Testing

Every change must be verified in **both single-player and a local multiplayer server** if
the mod has any code path that can run on either side — a mod's timed actions/events can run
server-side while the menu that created them ran client-side.

## 1. Deploy your working copy

```
mise run check             # lint + types first
mise run deploy client     # -> %USERPROFILE%\Zomboid\Workshop\__MOD_NAME__ (SP / client)
mise run deploy server     # -> .testhost\mods\__MOD_NAME__ (the ephemeral dedicated server)
mise run deploy all        # both
```

The target is **required** — a deploy never silently touches a location you didn't intend.
`client` feeds the "workshop (dev)" dir the game client loads from (enable the mod in the
in-game Mods list, Workshop tab). `server` feeds the ephemeral testhost (§2), *not* your real
`~\Zomboid` — your own installation never becomes the test playground.

